    <briefdescription>
<para>Rate-limiting decorator for contact-bounce suppression. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The first change of the underlying reading is accepted immediately; after that, further changes are ignored for tDebounceDelay ms. Readings taken during that window return the accepted value without polling the underlying reader.</para>
<para>Note: this is NOT a &quot;value must stay stable for tDebounceDelay ms&quot; debounce. Short glitches that occur right after an accepted change are filtered out by the lock window, but a glitch that arrives when no lock is active will be accepted as a new value.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>TReader</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Underlying reader type </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tDebounceDelay</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Lock window after an accepted change, ms </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
